25,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems our budget is under pressure. We are paying for empty space, and every single desk move carries a specific cost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that some areas are much noisier than others, and it takes a long time to get a chair and desk adjusted perfectly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"The morning setup takes more time than you'd think, and people arrive at very different times. It could be a mess.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The current plan ignores the daylight issue, which people hated. Also, unplanned shuffles in the past have been a total disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found that sitting close really helps. New joiners learn faster and we communicate better when we can just overhear things.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, if the morning routine is inefficient, we should avoid any layout that requires daily setup.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if moving desks is expensive, maybe we should just pick one spot and stay there?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, that sounds easier, but @Shunichi mentioned the daylight issue. We can't just ignore that people are unhappy.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. If we just ""stay put"" in a bad layout, we're just ignoring the problem. We need a system for the ""bad"" seats.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, but if we prioritize the ""bad"" seats too much, we might lose the benefit of sitting near the right people.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Victoria,,We must balance the financial cost of moving with the human cost of dissatisfaction.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried that if we move too often, I'll never get my workstation to feel right for my body.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I agree that communication is key, but not if it means wasting ten minutes every morning plugging in screens.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the financial cost is a factor, but the social cost of an unfair layout is what usually causes the shuffles.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just want us to be able to talk to each other without it being a chore.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
