55,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Looking at the options, Option C is a financial risk if it leads to more changes, but Option A is the most stable for the budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option C sounds terrible. I can't spend every day adjusting my chair and monitor. I need a permanent spot.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,Option C is a nightmare for my schedule. Spending nine minutes every morning just to start working is unacceptable.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is just a slow-motion version of the shuffles I read about. It doesn't solve the daylight inequality; it just rotates it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option A keeps us in groups, but Option C might let us mingle more. However, I worry about the stability.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, Option A allows us to group by function, which is cost-effective and prevents the chaos of free-addressing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Minato,,I strongly prefer Option A. It's the only way to ensure my physical comfort and a quiet environment.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,I'm with Minato. Option C is too time-consuming. Option B is just a hassle. Option A is the most efficient.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only one where we can explicitly decide who sits where to handle the window and noise issues.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If everyone else prefers Option A, and it keeps us in functional groups, I can support that.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Victoria,,It seems we have a consensus. Option A minimizes the facilities costs and provides the stability we need.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm relieved. I can finally have a spot that doesn't hurt my back or distract me with noise.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,No more morning screen-plugging marathons for me! I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"As long as we are honest about the seat assignments, Option A is the most rational choice. I vote A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for Option A too. Let's just make sure the groups are helpful for our work.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
